KG42.register("rules-01b44836bc87ab735dcf7e2a",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R021","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R021","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M04","name":"Energy-trade execution","process_stage":"activation","market_meaning":"TR counterparty selection limits executed trades to γ − 1 buyers and sellers, excluding buyer γ and seller γ. Scope: Trade Reduction auction restriction on the buyers and sellers permitted to trade.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function execution.energy_trade under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["execution.energy_trade","matching.counterparties"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R021-E001","source":"matching.counterparties","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R021-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Trade Reduction auction restriction on the buyers and sellers permitted to trade.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R021-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"TR counterparty selection limits executed trades to γ − 1 buyers and sellers, excluding buyer γ and seller γ. Scope: Trade Reduction auction restriction on the buyers and sellers permitted to trade.","expression":"|B_TR| = γ − 1 ∧ |S_TR| = γ − 1, where B_TR is the set of buyers permitted to execute trades and S_TR is the set of sellers permitted to execute trades under TR, and buyer γ ∉ B_TR ∧ seller γ ∉ S_TR (γ = largest breakeven buyer-seller index with B_γ^P ≥ S_γ^P)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-08","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M04-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to 1 Ta buyers and sellers [45]. Suc","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The Trade Reduction (TR) auction mechanism avoids subsidization of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to $\\gamma - 1$ buyers and sellers [45]. Such differs from uniform k-DA and VCG, where $\\gamma$ buyers and sellers are allowed to transact. Because buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted to participate in the TR auction, social welfare is not maximized. However, trading buyers pay $B_{\\gamma}^P$ and trading sellers receive $S_{\\gamma}^P$. As $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$, the market operator may financially gain $B_{\\gamma}^P - S_{\\gamma}^P$ from each single unit transaction."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"This rule is a mechanism-level restriction on counterparty selection, not an agent's optimization or operational decision. The source statement introduces no agent-controlled operational or design-selection variable; the only quantity, γ, is an endogenous index (the marginal / largest breakeven index), which is not a decision (x) variable. Hence x is empty.","empty_theta_reason":"The only symbol in the source statement, γ, is an index (the marginal buyer/seller index, defined in section 2.1 as the largest breakeven index satisfying B_γ^P ≥ S_γ^P), not a fixed numeric constant with a stated value. The source provides no constant input value for this rule, so θ is left empty rather than inventing a parameter value or domain; γ is referenced only within the rule-scoped expression."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M04-clearing","v141-a-M04-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-08","quote":"The Trade Reduction (TR) auction mechanism avoids subsidization of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to $\\gamma - 1$ buyers and sellers [45]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-08","quote":"buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted to participate in the TR auction"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"17f6c1cf4b6f17079cea81f1e9d00c3c772b7f625dbb2e1a585bc151e3f62ca0","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Rule v141-c-R021 encodes the Trade Reduction (TR) auction's mechanism-level restriction on which counterparties may reach trade execution. The only relevant evidence, v141-b-g01-ev-08 (UNREVIEWED in this experiment), states that TR 'avoid[s] subsidization of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to $\\gamma - 1$ buyers and sellers' and that 'buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted to participate in the TR auction'. This restriction is exactly the frozen graph relation matching.counterparties --limits--> execution.energy_trade (edge v141-c-R021-E001), so C001 is formalized as a cardinality-plus-exclusion condition on the executed counterparty set: exactly gamma - 1 buyers and gamma - 1 sellers trade, and the marginal pair (buyer gamma, seller gamma) is excluded. The symbol gamma is the source's marginal index (the largest breakeven index satisfying $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$, section 2.1); it is an index rather than a fixed numeric input, so theta is left empty and gamma is referenced only inside the scope of this rule's evidence. The restriction introduces no agent-controlled operational or design-selection variable, so x is empty. The formalization is provisional: B transcription and downstream science have not passed independent source review.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R021-C001","node_ids":["matching.counterparties","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R021-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is precisely the constraint carried by the frozen edge v141-c-R021-E001 (matching.counterparties --limits--> execution.energy_trade, evidence v141-b-g01-ev-08): counterparty selection (matching.counterparties) restricts the executed trades (execution.energy_trade) to gamma - 1 buyers and gamma - 1 sellers and excludes the marginal pair (buyer gamma, seller gamma). Both V nodes and the limiting edge are required to represent the restriction; the expression restates the same relation without adding any node or edge."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
